{"duration_api_ms": 105846, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "a9b36805-cd61-4e55-a8c5-4782b248b0c5", "total_cost_usd": 0.3580679, "usage": {"input_tokens": 18, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 42673, "cache_read_input_tokens": 312999, "output_tokens": 15604, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 4953}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 42673, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 452, "cache_read_input_tokens": 57501, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 328, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 328}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "modelUsage": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": {"inputTokens": 18, "outputTokens": 15604, "cacheReadInputTokens": 312999, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 42673, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.3580679, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 4953, "canonicalModel": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 10, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`.transform()` now carries CHECK constraints and column comments into the rebuilt table. The spec's check command passes (164 tests), and so does the full suite (1416 passed, 16 skipped).\n\n- **Parser:** the new `sqlite_utils/create_table_parser.py` has the lexer, `parse_checks`, `parse_column_comments`, `check_references_identifier`, `rewrite_check_expression`, `sql_ends_in_line_comment`, and the `Check`, `ColumnComments` and `ParseError` types.\n- **`db.py`:** `create_table_sql` takes `_checks` and `_column_comments`. `Table.checks`, `column_checks` and `table_checks` are added. `transform_sql` renames columns inside CHECK expressions and drops the checks and comments of dropped columns. It raises `TransformError` if a remaining check still uses a dropped column, or if the schema can't be parsed.\n\nOn the spec's open points, I chose these:\n- Table-level CHECKs go after the compound primary key clause, which is the last thing in the body.\n- An empty `IN ()` gives `options=[]`.\n- A double-quoted column name on the left side of `IN` still counts for `options`. Only a double-quoted identifier among the values rules it out.\n\nI did not touch docs, the changelog or the CLI, which the spec lists as out of scope.", "ttft_ms": 2025, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 115678, "uuid": "2092076f-5b8e-4151-aefb-924baba44187", "ttft_stream_ms": 1535, "time_to_request_ms": 54, "first_content_frame_ms": 1535, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
